1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,966
[beeping]

2
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:16,182
Oh no, I'm gonna be late!

3
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:18,435
[Anzu] Wait. What did I just say?

4
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:21,312
That phrase… It sounded so familiar.

5
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:22,939
[yelps]

6
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:25,942
[Hijiri] She's the one
who went running out into the street

7
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:27,444
right in front of us.

8
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:30,947
ONE WAY STREET

9
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,366
[officer] Please, miss,
be more aware of your surroundings.

10
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,409
[soft chuckle]

11
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:37,579
[Tsuchiya]
Let us give you a ride to school.

12
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:40,415
[car door closes]

13
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:44,753
[Anzu]
It seems like a pretty expensive car.

14
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:46,963
[car door closes]

15
00:00:47,046 --> 00:00:49,924
Hey, um, I'm really sorry
that I made you late.

16
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:52,135
Having a couple of tardies?

17
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:56,014
That won't affect my report card.
I'm an excellent student.

18
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:59,476
[Anzu] Anyway,
why would a rich kid like him

19
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,186
go to a public school?

20
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:04,022
He's good-looking
but I haven't seen him before.

21
00:01:04,606 --> 00:01:06,441
Well, you must be ecstatic.

22
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:10,945
I mean, getting the chance
to ride to school with me and everything.

23
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:13,031
[Hijiri] You should be grateful.

24
00:01:13,114 --> 00:01:13,948
[grunts]

25
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:18,870
[Anzu in deep voice] Hang on, Anzu,
don't punch him in the face.

26
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:22,832
Hold it in. This all happened
because I was being careless.

27
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:26,836
[in normal voice]
Oh. Both Kazuki and Saki messaged me.

28
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,754
TSUKASA: YOU GOOD?

29
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:29,047
I should respond.

30
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,341
I GOT IN A MINOR ACCIDENT,
BUT I'M OKAY.

31
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:38,139
[theme music]

32
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:02,223
[school bell dings]

33
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:05,727
#7: WHAT A STRONG PERSONALITY

34
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:08,313
[indistinct chatter]

35
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,857
[Anzu] Great, just in time for break.

36
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:15,820
Uh, this is me right here.

37
00:03:16,404 --> 00:03:18,865
[Hijiri] You exchanged contacts
with Tsuchiya, right?

38
00:03:18,948 --> 00:03:19,782
Hmm?

39
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:21,910
-[Tsuchiya] My name is Tsuchiya.
-Oh, yeah.

40
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:25,330
[Hijiri] I'll be in touch at a later day.
You just wait.

41
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:28,207
And enjoy dreaming about me.

42
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:32,420
[Anzu] Seriously?
There's still more to talk about?

43
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:35,673
-Hmm?
-[gasps]

44
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:36,591
Oh…

45
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:40,345
Anzu! Why did you arrive
with Mr. Hijiri Koganei?

46
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:41,262
Mister?

47
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:43,848
Anzu, are… are you sure
that you're not hurt?

48
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:45,266
Yeah, thank you, Saki.

49
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:47,310
[gasps]
You are so lucky!

50
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:50,021
-[exclaims]
-You got hit by Mr. Hijiri's car.

51
00:03:50,104 --> 00:03:51,773
[Anzu] Why do you keep saying "Mister"?

52
00:03:51,856 --> 00:03:52,774
What do you mean?

53
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:55,735
He's Mr. Hijiri Koganei,
the rich star from Class 8!

54
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:58,112
He is like a prince.
He even has his own fan club.

55
00:03:58,196 --> 00:03:59,030
PRINCE HIJIRI

56
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:00,865
I see…

57
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:03,034
[Anzu] I mean, it seems obvious,

58
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:06,537
but, this has got to be
another one of their setups!

59
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:08,498
-[Anzu] I got to get up…
-And insert!

60
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:11,417
-[Anzu] I'll be late…
-Now she'll be running really late!

61
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:12,835
-[Makoto] Hosshi!
-[Junta] Anzu!

62
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:14,045
Oh!

63
00:04:14,128 --> 00:04:17,131
-Are you okay? We heard you got hit!
-Anzu, I was worried about you.

64
00:04:18,132 --> 00:04:19,425
[in high-pitched voice]
Hayami! Oh gosh!

65
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:22,512
-You're not hurt at all, are you?
-Nope. I'm all good.

66
00:04:23,096 --> 00:04:24,138
[sighs]

67
00:04:25,056 --> 00:04:27,558
I bet you were rushing
and ran into the street.

68
00:04:27,642 --> 00:04:28,768
Yeah.

69
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:31,479
Still, I really think
you should go to the hospital.

70
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:33,231
The car barely hit me, though.

71
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:35,483
Hosshi, you and Hayami are friends?

72
00:04:35,566 --> 00:04:36,901
Nice!

73
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:39,946
He's, um, he's an "old friend,"
quote unquote.

74
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:41,364
-Let's go.
-[squeals]

75
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:43,741
Let me know if anything starts hurting,
all right?

76
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:45,243
[Anzu] Okay, thanks.

77
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:48,496
[sighs]
This is so incredibly unfair,

78
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:49,539
I can't even…

79
00:04:49,622 --> 00:04:52,667
Both of those heartthrobs are just
so worried about you.

80
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:56,045
Well, actually,
Kazuki wasn't worried about me at all.

81
00:04:59,048 --> 00:05:01,968
A FEW DAYS LATER.

82
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:04,929
[Anzu] Maybe I'm a little early.

83
00:05:08,057 --> 00:05:11,060
[Tsuchiya] Would this coming Saturday
work for you?

84
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:14,355
[Anzu] What else is left to go over?

85
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:16,482
[car approaching]

86
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:21,487
[Hijiri scoffs]
You're extremely early.

87
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:25,992
You wanted to see me so bad
you've been waiting here since last night?

88
00:05:27,535 --> 00:05:29,996
You really are something else, aren't you?

89
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:32,874
[forced laugh]
Oh yeah, I've been waiting all night.

90
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,501
Held strong,
like I was defending the Alamo.

91
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:37,837
Whatever.

92
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:40,214
What's with the peasant look
you've got on?

93
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:42,884
[Hijiri] How could you even stand
next to me dressed like that?

94
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:44,302
Are you trying to insult me?

95
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:46,763
-[angry meow]
-[grunts]

96
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:51,392
[Anzu] I humbly apologize.
I'm just a low-born villager NPC

97
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:53,853
in a game, repeating the same line
over and over again.

98
00:05:53,936 --> 00:05:54,771
VILLAGER A

99
00:05:55,354 --> 00:05:57,398
[scoffs]
Whatever.

100
00:05:58,107 --> 00:05:59,025
-[Hijiri] Get in.
-Huh?

101
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:00,401
[yelps]

102
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,028
[groans]

103
00:06:02,111 --> 00:06:05,031
-You lack sincerity.
-[growls]

104
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:09,535
With all my attention,
you'll be our school's Cinderella.

105
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,790
[Anzu] Wanted:
Someone to translate for this guy.

106
00:06:16,876 --> 00:06:17,960
[Anzu] Well…

107
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:21,589
[magical music]

108
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:29,889
-What the heck am I doing here?
-Aah…

109
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:32,892
Hmm. Now you're decent.

110
00:06:33,392 --> 00:06:35,812
And now I wanna know what's happening.

111
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:40,024
-Get her some flat shoes.
-[approaching footsteps]

112
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,692
[Hijiri] Why are you unnecessarily tall?

113
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:44,153
Maybe I should give you
some of my height, then.

114
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:49,117
-[Hijiri] Okay, let's go to lunch.
-Huh? Whoa, wait, what?

115
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,244
Go to lunch, why?

116
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:55,164
[Hijiri] I'm really pushed for time here.

117
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:57,667
-Tell me what's going on!
-We're doing French.

118
00:06:57,750 --> 00:07:00,169
[groans]
I don't need lunch!

119
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:04,799
I don't get why you think it's okay
to make me over like that!

120
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:06,843
It's entirely your fault

121
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:10,304
for showing up on a date with me
dressed like a poor being.

122
00:07:10,888 --> 00:07:12,557
What are you talking about, date?

123
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:15,017
Aren't we meeting 'cause I got hit?

124
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:16,227
No need to play dumb.

125
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:19,856
You purposefully got hit
in order to get closer to me, right?

126
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:21,649
Huh?

127
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:26,863
Cars are legally at fault
when they hit pedestrians.

128
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:30,324
You took advantage of that
so you could go out with me, didn't you?

129
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:33,119
You actually think
that I staged the accident?

130
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:35,705
-Oh, did you not?
-Not at all, no!

131
00:07:35,788 --> 00:07:37,457
Idiots like that exist?

132
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:40,001
It's happened countless times
since preschool.

133
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:41,502
So several exist, then.

134
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:44,338
Tsuchiya's driver's license is
on a permanent watchlist now.

135
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:45,882
[Tsuchiya] It was suspended once too.

136
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:48,885
[Anzu] You poor thing.
I'm really, really sorry!

137
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:52,597
Anyway, I'm not one of those girls, and I,

138
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,724
I can't accept these clothes.

139
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:55,892
I'll pay for them.

140
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:58,728
Nine hundred dollars, just for the dress.

141
00:07:58,811 --> 00:07:59,645
[yelps]

142
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:01,647
Is it made out of an ancient relic silk
or something?

143
00:08:01,731 --> 00:08:02,815
YOU OBTAINED ANCIENT THREADS!

144
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:04,233
Whatever.

145
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:07,278
Intentional or no,
it was still an accident.

146
00:08:08,404 --> 00:08:11,699
You received clothes and you're also
about to have lunch with me.

147
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:14,452
Think of it as a peasant's godsend.

148
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:17,330
[groaning]

149
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:19,916
[Anzu] Mr. Tsuchiya, please stop.

150
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:23,628
What now?

151
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:25,922
I feel bad
that you did all of this for me.

152
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:29,342
-Whoa? Huh?
-[accessories jingle]

153
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:32,470
I'm not at all interested in you.

154
00:08:32,553 --> 00:08:33,596
[gasps]

155
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:36,307
[Anzu] So there's no need for us
to waste each other's time.

156
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:38,643
See ya.

157
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:41,479
[retreating footsteps]

158
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:45,191
[Anzu] Being manipulated
by an extremely full of himself rich kid

159
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:46,108
is really annoying,

160
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:49,278
especially when he's got
a stuck-up attitude like that.

161
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,489
But the most frustrating thing is

162
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:55,243
he actually thought
I was one of those idiots

163
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,870
who would stage an accident for a date!

164
00:08:57,954 --> 00:08:59,622
[men laughing]

165
00:08:59,705 --> 00:09:03,209
[Anzu in deep voice] I belong
to a warrior race that forges its way down

166
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:06,295
the exact opposite path of life
every single day!

167
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:09,507
[screams, heavy breathing]

168
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:13,135
[Anzu] Damn, my pits are sweating
all over this 900-dollar dress.

169
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,638
THIS IS A ROMANTIC ANIME

170
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:21,352
She has no interest in me?

171
00:09:22,478 --> 00:09:25,398
[birds chirping]

172
00:09:27,483 --> 00:09:29,026
HIJIRI LOVE

173
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:31,779
-That's not good. Mr. Hijiri looks sad.
-[girls swooning]

174
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,490
But he looks so fragile and beautiful.

175
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:36,993
[approaching footsteps]

176
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:37,910
Huh?

177
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,538
Hijiri Koganei.

178
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:43,165
Uh, it's you.

179
00:09:43,749 --> 00:09:46,502
Address me respectfully. That was rude.

180
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,796
[sighs]
Are you kidding me?

181
00:09:48,879 --> 00:09:51,841
[scoffs]
What do you want anyway?

182
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:54,385
Trying to make up
for being rude the other day?

183
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:57,513
[Anzu] I dry-cleaned the clothes,
so I just wanted to return them to you.

184
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:58,598
Goodbye.

185
00:09:58,681 --> 00:09:59,807
[retreating footsteps]

186
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:05,438
[Hijiri] She certainly left in a hurry

187
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:08,482
after going out of her way
to return the gifts I gave her.

188
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:13,195
There's no need
to worry about that peasant.

189
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:16,782
But the way she's been giving me
all of that attitude…

190
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:19,452
[sinister music]

191
00:10:19,535 --> 00:10:20,911
[Hijiri] I don't like it one bit.

192
00:10:23,247 --> 00:10:26,042
Tsuchiya, I need something investigated.

193
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:28,127
[cheerful music]

194
00:10:29,128 --> 00:10:31,005
[Junta humming]

195
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:33,591
Junta, you're chipper.

196
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:36,594
Wednesday means no club,
so I get to walk home with you.

197
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,346
Oh, okay, I see.

198
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,181
Kazuki has work today, right?

199
00:10:40,264 --> 00:10:42,516
Yeah. What should we do for dinner?

200
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:46,103
It might be terrible,
but I can make us something.

201
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:48,606
Really? You would? I'll eat it!

202
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,652
You know, maybe I should learn
how to cook myself.

203
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:54,487
I only know how to make ramen.

204
00:10:54,987 --> 00:10:56,989
You should just focus on your baseball.

205
00:10:57,615 --> 00:11:00,326
[Anzu] He's such a good guy
compared to that other one.

206
00:11:00,409 --> 00:11:04,205
I hope Junta finds happiness
with someone he truly loves.

207
00:11:04,288 --> 00:11:07,792
But for that to happen,
I really need to do something about them.

208
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:09,001
-[Riri] Anzu!
-[blows air]

209
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:12,088
I wanna come too! Can I come for dinner?

210
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:14,006
[Anzu] Maybe I should just give her
a quick death.

211
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:15,508
[Anzu] Honestly, how dare you?

212
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:18,302
Why send such a ridiculous character?

213
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:20,096
There's no way I'd fall for him!

214
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:23,516
Oh, when I'm in this form,
everybody can see and hear us.

215
00:11:23,599 --> 00:11:24,517
[giggles]

216
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:29,188
Well, I'm not a very good cook,
so you should probably just go home.

217
00:11:29,271 --> 00:11:31,524
-Not letting go of that grip, then?
-Hmm?

218
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:34,527
[Junta] Uh…

219
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,112
-[car door opens]
-[both] Huh?

220
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:38,531
Anzu Hoshino.

221
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:40,157
-Not him.
-[chuckles]

222
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:44,161
You're the first woman to say
that you have no interest in me at all.

223
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:46,163
I'm intrigued.

224
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:49,917
Just know
that I'll steal your heart eventually.

225
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:52,837
-Heh.
-[squeals]

226
00:11:56,298 --> 00:11:58,217
-Aren't you starving?
-Mm-hm.

227
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,220
-[Riri] Oh, jeez. My stomach just rumbled…
-Goodness. Such a cramped place.

228
00:12:01,303 --> 00:12:04,473
-Oh! So, Junta…
-I'm sure it is for you, Mr. Prince.

229
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:06,851
-[Hijiri] By the way, who are these two?
-[both] Huh?

230
00:12:06,934 --> 00:12:09,019
[Hijiri] My business is only with Hoshino.

231
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:09,937
[Junta sighs]

232
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:12,606
I'm Riri, Anzu's cousin.

233
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:16,360
And this is one of her oldest friends
from childhood, Junta.

234
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:19,613
The three of us will be having dinner
together tonight.

235
00:12:19,697 --> 00:12:21,449
You can actually leave now.

236
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,451
So…

237
00:12:24,034 --> 00:12:26,704
What's this business?
Some more lame stuff?

238
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:29,039
[Hijiri] Tsuchiya.

239
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:29,999
Yes, sir.

240
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:34,962
-Huh? Hmm…
-Miss Hoshino, this is for you.

241
00:12:37,548 --> 00:12:38,466
[Anzu] Huh?

242
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:41,469
[Anzu] It's a Skitch! And a VR headset!

243
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:44,680
The chocolates are all fancy brands!

244
00:12:45,764 --> 00:12:48,100
[squealing]

245
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:50,060
-[Tsuchiya] And that's not all, miss.
-Huh?

246
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:51,979
[Anzu yelps]

247
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:55,983
-[meowing]
-[Anzu whimpers]

248
00:13:01,071 --> 00:13:03,908
[Anzu] Destruction level: severe.

249
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:04,992
[meowing]

250
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:08,996
Well, you appear
to be satisfied with my gifts.

251
00:13:09,079 --> 00:13:10,998
[Anzu] That came out of nowhere.

252
00:13:11,081 --> 00:13:14,585
Did he actually feel bad
about me getting upset?

253
00:13:15,085 --> 00:13:18,964
Along with great elegance
and my appearance which exudes charm,

254
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:23,260
I have the financial power
to make your every wish come true.

255
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,596
[gasps]

256
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:27,640
You're interested in me now, right?

257
00:13:27,723 --> 00:13:30,017
Oh, so it's that kind of scenario.

258
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:33,479
Tell me, how did you find out
about my favorite things?

259
00:13:33,562 --> 00:13:35,231
Anything's possible for me.

260
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:36,899
No, an actual answer.

261
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:42,321
[Anzu] It really bothered you when I said
I wasn't interested in you, didn't it?

262
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:44,114
[Anzu grunts]

263
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:47,034
-[in deep voice] Well, guess what? Hey!
-Stop right there!

264
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:50,538
Anzu, hon, I just need
a quick word with you for a second!

265
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:57,294
I know that we confiscated
your three greatest desires,

266
00:13:57,378 --> 00:14:00,548
but it would be very rude
of you to reject his gifts.

267
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:02,925
I will allow 'em,

268
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:05,553
but here's the catch for accepting them!

269
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:07,263
What, are you serious?

270
00:14:07,346 --> 00:14:08,556
You can only keep 'em

271
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:12,017
if you allow a relationship
to develop with Hijiri Koganei.

272
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:13,561
[sighs]

273
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:18,941
-[Anzu] If I start dating him…
-[arrogant laughter]

274
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:23,237
…I can enjoy all those gifts right now.

275
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:26,365
[kittens meowing]

276
00:14:28,742 --> 00:14:31,245
What are those two
talking about out there?

277
00:14:31,328 --> 00:14:33,038
Who… who knows?

278
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:34,999
[sighs]

279
00:14:35,082 --> 00:14:38,043
Um, your name was Koganei?

280
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:39,628
That's informal and rude.

281
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:42,506
Oh, sorry, Mr. Koganei.

282
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:45,759
I heard about the accident
with Anzu and everything.

283
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:49,013
But, um, well, do you, um…

284
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:53,017
[Junta] Anzu, uh, do you like her?

285
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:56,604
Like her?

286
00:14:58,022 --> 00:15:01,025
That's not an emotion
I'd feel for anyone at all.

287
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:04,528
That's an emotion
everyone else feels for me.

288
00:15:05,362 --> 00:15:06,530
Right.

289
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:10,284
But Hoshino's stated
that she has absolutely no interest in me.

290
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:12,453
It's a serious matter.

291
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:15,539
[Junta] I see.
That's why you're doing all this.

292
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:20,920
Just so you know, Anzu won't become
your friend just because…

293
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:23,505
you're rich or you're good-looking.

294
00:15:25,132 --> 00:15:26,008
Hmm?

295
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,052
[slaps]

296
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:31,472
[Anzu] You're completely clueless
about humans.

297
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:35,726
Setting up forced encounters
and messing with emotions,

298
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:38,062
now luring me in with my desires.

299
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:42,441
I'm no fool.

300
00:15:45,110 --> 00:15:45,945
Oh.

301
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:49,949
-Please leave. I don't want this stuff.
-How could…

302
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:52,952
[Anzu] I'm incredibly sorry
if I hurt your pride,

303
00:15:53,535 --> 00:15:55,955
but you'll have to find someone else
to fawn over you.

304
00:15:56,622 --> 00:16:00,501
And since you're human,
you understand feelings.

305
00:16:00,584 --> 00:16:01,543
Right, Hijiri?

306
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:05,089
[Anzu] And another thing,
there's no point strutting around

307
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:07,257
promising my every wish
with your parents' money.

308
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:09,760
It's okay when it's money
you earn yourself.

309
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:12,972
And above all…

310
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:17,977
If you don't have Momohiki,
then you don't have a chance!

311
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:21,981
[sighs]

312
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:24,066
[exhales sharply]

313
00:16:25,567 --> 00:16:28,070
[huffs, sighs]

314
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:34,493
That was interesting.

315
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:37,121
Junta…

316
00:16:37,204 --> 00:16:39,790
[Anzu]
If I had accepted Riri's conditions,

317
00:16:39,873 --> 00:16:42,960
would they have released Junta
from the love spell?

318
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:44,336
[exhales sharply]

319
00:16:45,295 --> 00:16:47,047
I'm sorry you're involved with this.

320
00:16:47,631 --> 00:16:49,508
Don't be. I'm just fine.

321
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:53,512
If you're ever in trouble,
please just let me know.

322
00:16:55,556 --> 00:16:56,515
[whimpers]

323
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:00,019
[Anzu] He's too good of a person
it's painful.

324
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:02,521
[chuckles]

325
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:06,900
Hey Anzu, how come
you're playing with him anyway?

326
00:17:07,526 --> 00:17:09,611
Yeah, I won't let you play my new game.

327
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:13,032
What? You suck.

328
00:17:13,115 --> 00:17:17,619
-[Junta] Uh, are you sure?
-It's okay. Those guys are all talk.

329
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:21,290
And I had plans to hang with you first.

330
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:24,793
How come you kicked him out, huh?

331
00:17:24,877 --> 00:17:26,545
I really want to kick you out.

332
00:17:26,628 --> 00:17:28,589
-[Riri] Not nice!
-[chuckles]

333
00:17:29,631 --> 00:17:31,383
DONUTS

334
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:32,551
[rustling]

335
00:17:32,634 --> 00:17:33,927
[sighs]

336
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:37,514
[manager] Miss Hoshino,
we've got a new employee starting today.

337
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:38,724
Oh, right.

338
00:17:40,017 --> 00:17:40,934
[Anzu] What?

339
00:17:41,852 --> 00:17:43,103
[manager] This is Mr. Koganei.

340
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:45,189
[bright music]

341
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:47,983
Yes, I'm here to learn.
You should have no issues.

342
00:17:48,525 --> 00:17:50,444
CONBINI MART
SEASONAL SWEETS

343
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,404
Welcome in.

344
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:57,951
I appreciate that.

345
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:01,080
Come again.

346
00:18:01,663 --> 00:18:03,749
Hey!

347
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:05,793
How many meters above us are you?

348
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:07,753
Excuse you, millions of meters.

349
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,755
Orbitally higher?

350
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:12,299
You think that's good customer service?

351
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:13,759
She's right.

352
00:18:14,551 --> 00:18:16,011
It's better if you add,

353
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:19,264
"But I won't actually wait for you"
after "Come again."

354
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:21,767
[Anzu]
Don't encourage the hot and cold thing!

355
00:18:23,018 --> 00:18:25,562
Manager, sir, are you sure about this?

356
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:27,773
Hmm, well, thing is…

357
00:18:27,856 --> 00:18:28,816
[device beeps]

358
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:31,151
-Shall I warm it?
-Oh, yes.

359
00:18:31,235 --> 00:18:34,488
[manager] The customers all seem
to be attracted to Mr. Koganei's aura,

360
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:36,073
so there haven't been any complaints.

361
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:38,784
[Anzu]
But he's inconsiderate and obnoxious!

362
00:18:40,702 --> 00:18:44,206
Hijiri went viral,
known as the convenience store prince.

363
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:48,710
The #storeprince spread
like wildfire all over social media…

364
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:50,254
SEASONAL SWEETS NOW AVAILABLE

365
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:52,714
…and attracted a whole lot of customers!

366
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:55,217
[customers whispering]

367
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:57,177
Mm-hm.

368
00:18:58,303 --> 00:19:04,226
AVAILABLE NATIONWIDE

369
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:07,229
Your change. Do come again.

370
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:08,564
Thanks.

371
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:09,690
[Anzu grumbles]

372
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:12,651
[Anzu] I guess he must've ended up
with that attitude

373
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:15,737
because everyone around him
seems to enable him.

374
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,740
But he is a fast learner,

375
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:21,076
and he doesn't ask for time off.

376
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,495
-And to be honest, he does work hard.
-Welcome in.

377
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:27,332
-You can take your break now.
-Mm-hm.

378
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:29,168
[chuckles]

379
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:31,253
Wait, is the Prince going on break?

380
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,256
Sorry about that.
[chuckles awkwardly]

381
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:37,259
CONBINI MART

382
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:41,763
[moans]
I'm so tired.

383
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:44,016
Oh, Mr. Tsuchiya.

384
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,895
Good evening, miss.

385
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:50,397
Hi there. Hijiri will be out in a sec.

386
00:19:53,066 --> 00:19:54,026
Miss Hoshino.

387
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:58,113
I don't know how to express the gratitude
I have for what you have done.

388
00:19:58,780 --> 00:19:59,781
What?

389
00:20:00,949 --> 00:20:05,537
Mr. Hijiri, he attended an expensive
escalator-styled private school,

390
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:07,039
but due to his father's wishes,

391
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:09,791
he was enrolled at the school
where you currently attend.

392
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:11,043
Oh.

393
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:12,961
[Tsuchiya] His loved ones
are enamored with him,

394
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:16,215
and he always got anything
and everything he wanted growing up,

395
00:20:16,298 --> 00:20:18,884
so he can be a bit out of touch,
and he lacks common sense.

396
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:19,801
Hmm…

397
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:22,930
His father became concerned about that,

398
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:25,098
so he decided that he wanted Hijiri

399
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:27,768
to experience a normal life
at a normal school.

400
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:31,271
[Tsuchiya] However, his innate
and inherent heir of nobility

401
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:33,815
has always made him feel
above everything normal.

402
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:35,817
Right.

403
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:40,405
But now, because you had the ability
to reason with him directly…

404
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:44,326
First, I hit the bottom right key there.
And then I enter…

405
00:20:44,409 --> 00:20:49,248
[Tsuchiya] Mr. Hijiri has actually been
trying to learn more about normal life.

406
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:52,584
This is all your doing.

407
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:54,586
Thank you so very much.

408
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:56,213
Oh, of course.

409
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:58,590
[chuckles]

410
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:03,595
NARIKIN BANK

411
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:05,597
BANK ACCOUNT
ORDINARY FINANCIALS

412
00:21:05,681 --> 00:21:06,598
[squeals, gasps]

413
00:21:07,182 --> 00:21:08,558
My paycheck!

414
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:12,437
I'm so glad. How should I spend it? Hmm…

415
00:21:12,521 --> 00:21:14,314
[chuckles]

416
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:16,233
-[Hijiri] Hoshino.
-[gasps]

417
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:18,318
[shrieks]

418
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:22,072
Jeez, Hijiri!
There's no work today, is there?

419
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:23,782
Then why are you following me?

420
00:21:23,865 --> 00:21:27,327
How rude. I just happened to see you
so I called your name.

421
00:21:28,036 --> 00:21:29,830
I received my paycheck today.

422
00:21:29,913 --> 00:21:32,541
So, Hoshino, what do you want?

423
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:34,042
Huh?

424
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:36,837
It's only a few days' worth
so it can't be too great,

425
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:39,548
but I'm sure I can fulfill anything
your peasant heart desires.

426
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:42,551
And I earned the money all on my own.

427
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:45,554
But don't get the wrong idea.

428
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:47,097
[Hijiri chuckles dryly]

429
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:51,852
It's not like
I did any of this stuff for you.

430
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:55,439
[Anzu] That hot and cold personality
was implanted in him.

431
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:57,107
What do you want?

432
00:21:57,190 --> 00:22:00,277
-A bag? Some shoes?
-No, no, thanks.

433
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:02,612
-Some jewelry?
-No, no, no, no.

434
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:04,489
Instead of a gift,
would you prefer a date?

435
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:05,449
Please, shut up!

436
00:22:05,532 --> 00:22:08,869
[Anzu] As much as I want to say
I don't want a thing from him…

437
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:11,455
[soft piano music]

438
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,126
Hmm.

439
00:22:16,209 --> 00:22:19,379
Oh! All right, I know what I want.

440
00:22:22,841 --> 00:22:23,925
[Anzu chuckles]

441
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:26,970
What in the world is that?

442
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,972
Pipiko. You wouldn't know.

443
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:32,934
It was surprisingly cheap,
even for a peasant's item.

444
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:34,394
-[snaps]
-Hmm?

445
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:36,897
[Anzu] Here. That's your half.

446
00:22:40,108 --> 00:22:41,902
Thank you for the treat.
[chuckles]

447
00:22:42,736 --> 00:22:44,488
You're happy with something like this?

448
00:22:45,489 --> 00:22:48,492
Well yeah, I think it's the perfect thing
to share with friends.

449
00:22:48,992 --> 00:22:50,077
[exclaims]

450
00:22:56,792 --> 00:22:57,751
What do you think?

451
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:01,338
It tastes artificial and cheap.

452
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:05,050
But it's, it's not bad.

453
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:07,385
[magical music]

454
00:23:08,011 --> 00:23:08,887
[gasps]

455
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:11,306
[yelps, grunts]

456
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:12,808
What's wrong?

457
00:23:13,391 --> 00:23:15,811
Getting back my sanity. That's all.

458
00:23:16,895 --> 00:23:17,813
[Anzu grunts]

459
00:23:19,356 --> 00:23:21,441
[Anzu]
This might have been a huge mistake.

460
00:23:23,401 --> 00:23:25,320
[scrubbing]

461
00:23:28,406 --> 00:23:29,908
[door opens]

462
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:34,162
I'm home, guys.

463
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:36,331
[phone chimes, vibrates]

464
00:23:37,916 --> 00:23:38,917
What?

465
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:39,835
ARISA
CAN WE MEET?

466
00:23:39,918 --> 00:23:40,961
[Anzu] It's Kazuki's phone.

467
00:23:41,044 --> 00:23:42,337
ARISA
CAN WE MEET?

468
00:23:42,420 --> 00:23:46,341
[Anzu gasps]
It's a girl!

469
00:23:48,802 --> 00:23:50,554
A fanfare, please!

470
00:23:50,637 --> 00:23:52,639
And a big congratulations!

471
00:23:52,722 --> 00:23:55,016
Did you fall for my little trick?

472
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:58,061
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

473
00:23:58,145 --> 00:24:01,815
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

474
00:24:01,898 --> 00:24:04,568
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

475
00:24:04,651 --> 00:24:06,945
[sighs]
Don't just let things be! Come on!

476
00:24:07,028 --> 00:24:09,698
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

477
00:24:09,781 --> 00:24:11,616
So I can make sure I get paid.

478
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:13,869
[closing theme music]

479
00:24:13,952 --> 00:24:14,786
♪ Ah, yeah! ♪

480
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:18,248
♪ Let's go! ♪

481
00:24:20,667 --> 00:24:21,793
♪ Lo-love! ♪

482
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:24,838
♪ Here we go! ♪
